WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.420
Safe apps, safe money, safe files, and smooth online classes.

2
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.600
This is the video for module four: apps, money and everyday online tools.

3
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:19.720
Get apps only from the Play Store, and look before you tap Install. Tap the developer name. A real bank app is published by the bank itself.

4
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:27.670
Read the most recent reviews, not just the stars. Many complaints about stolen money are a clear warning.

5
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.060
Scroll to Data safety to see what the app collects.

6
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:41.330
A calculator does not need your contacts. A loan app that wants your contacts and photos may use them to shame you to your family.

7
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:51.920
Ngozi in Owerri found three apps with her bank's logo. She opened the bank's official website, tapped its Play Store link, and installed the genuine one.

8
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:58.390
And never install APK files sent on WhatsApp. Keep Install unknown apps switched off.

9
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:07.520
Most money lost online is not lost because criminals broke the bank. They trick someone, or take control of their phone number.

10
00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:11.620
First, they gather your details from phishing or social media.

11
00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:17.670
Then they get someone at a network outlet to move your number onto their new SIM.

12
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:24.530
Your phone shows No service for a long time, while people near you on the same network have signal.

13
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:30.520
Now your bank codes go to the criminal, who can reset passwords and move your money.

14
00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:40.560
Step one. Borrow another phone and call your network's customer care. Report a possible SIM swap and ask them to block the number.

15
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:47.080
Step two. Call your bank's official number and ask them to freeze your account and cards.

16
00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.810
Step three. Change your email password, because email is used to reset bank logins.

17
00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:02.140
Step four. Visit your network's office with your ID to recover your number, and report the fraud to your bank in writing.

18
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.100
Step five. Write down times, calls and reference numbers.

19
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:17.630
Prepare today. During a SIM swap your phone may not work, so save your bank's fraud line and emergency block code in your contacts, and on paper at home.

20
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:24.620
Hauwa in Jos is selling two bags of rice. The buyer shows her a screenshot of a transfer.

21
00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:34.780
He says he sent 38,000 naira. Then he says he sent 83,000 by mistake, and asks her to refund 45,000.

22
00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:46.660
Hauwa does not trust screenshots or SMS. She opens her own bank app. No money arrived at all. She keeps her rice, refunds nothing, and warns the other traders.

23
00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:54.410
Trust only the balance inside your own bank app. And never tell anyone your PIN, OTP, password or BVN.

24
00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:06.330
Use a transaction PIN that is different from your phone lock and ATM PIN, turn on fingerprint login, and set a daily limit that matches what you really send.

25
00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:18.950
Do not use your birthday or 1234. Read every debit alert. And always read the account name before you confirm, so money does not go to the wrong person.

26
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:29.630
Google Drive keeps your files online, safe even if your phone is lost. Tap plus, then Scan, to turn a certificate into a clean PDF.

27
00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:39.130
Joy in Calabar applied for a job from her phone. She scanned her documents, and shared each one as Viewer with the employer's email.

28
00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:49.750
She kept General access as Restricted, so only the employer could open them. Anyone with the link means anyone who gets it forwarded can open it.

29
00:03:51.000 --> 00:04:04.630
Mercy in Uyo joined her first WODDI Institute class on Google Meet. She installed the app at midday, charged her phone, sat near a window for 4G, and joined early with her microphone and camera off.

30
00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:14.410
She used the chat and raised her hand. Never post meeting links publicly, and an interview that asks for a fee or your ATM card is a scam.

31
00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:24.470
To remember. Check the developer, and never install APKs. If your SIM loses service while others have signal, act at once.

32
00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:31.410
Trust only your bank app balance. Share files as Viewer and Restricted. And keep meeting links private.

33
00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:43.180
Now practise. Run Play Protect, write your emergency card with your bank and network numbers, build a safe document folder, and hold a practice call with a friend.

34
00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.470
Continue with the lessons below.
